<div class="content-box" style="background: #fff3cd; border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;">
    <h2><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Watch Out For</h2>
    <p>Common misconceptions to avoid:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Binary Search: Students often forget that Binary Search requires a sorted list to function.</li>
        <li>Sorting Efficiency: Believing Bubble Sort is "good" because it's easy to write, without understanding its $O(n^2)$ limitation.</li>
        <li>File I/O: Forgetting to .close() a file or confusing 'w' (overwrite) with 'a' (append) modes.</li>
        <li>Loops: Infinite loops caused by incorrect termination conditions in while structures.</li>
    </ul>
</div>

